WEBVTT

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.020
The following tale is a work of pure fiction.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.770
<b>June 1582 {ts}</b>

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.770
<b>Horagatouge Pass {ts}</b>

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.940
Curse that Tsutsui Junkei!

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.820
The lout pledges his forces to Milord for taking the Kawachi Province,

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.620
and dispatches not a single man!

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:26.560
Retain naught but the allegiance of the Imperial Court and temples!

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.950
Milord!

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:34.330
Scouts from Kawachi and Settsu report sighting Hashiba's forces garrison Amagasaki Castle.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.260
'Tis naught but a ploy of Hashiba's.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.920
From Takamatsu Castle, the winds may usher the swift return of a few, though not of a force.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.060
Though General Hashiba retained not my absolute trust,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.530
all is well. {maa yoi}

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.150
Should he surrender, lenience unto him.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.430
Should he resist, Death unto him!

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:02.270
G-General Hashiba's garrison numbers 10,000, exceeding our force!

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:03.940
How can this be?!

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.680
'Twas that of a complete withdrawal from Takamatsu Castle!

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.960
General Hashiba's forces raise a banner of queer nature to signify their intentions to avenge Nobunaga!

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.460
<b>Aesthete's Roast {ts}</b>

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.550
Make haste!

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.030
Hashiba's forces shall soon march on Kyoto!

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:35.300
Rally our forces south to Shimotoba, and we shall meet Hashiba's forces at the entry of Kyoto, Oyamazaki!

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:42.750
'Tis a deed of the gods to withdraw over 10,000 so swiftly within so few days! {from arienu until koto nado}

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.360
Though...

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:50.860
had he prepared prior to our assault on Honno Temple...

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.020
Had I one wish though...

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:04.400
'twould be to serve a virtuous man alike yourself.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.190
Deceived...

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:20.850
Deceived by a veil of tears, for Hashiba intended the subjugation of the realm! {until minukenu to wa}

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.850
'Twas I who was deceived... {until hashiba ni}

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.900
by Hashiba Hideyoshi!

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.530
<b>June 12, 1582 {ts}</b>

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.530
<b>Mikawa Province Okazaki Castle {ts}</b>

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.880
General Hashiba's forces in Settsu hold Amagasaki Castle with over 10,000.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.260
Soon, his main forces shall march on Kyoto and clash with General Akechi's forces.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.300
Preposterous...

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:59.820
How may so large a force march so swift?!

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.140
Such maneuvers imply Hashiba's prior knowledge of General Akechi's rebellion.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:06.370
'Tis not his maneuvers which bewitch my eyes, but this banner!

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.190
Dare they attempt to avenge Oda Nobunaga under so absurd a banner?!

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.470
Know not the sanity of its maker!

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:16.290
Regardless, Hashiba's vengeance is naught but mere pretense to conquer the realm!

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.180
Indeed, Tadakatsu.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:23.650
I behold not a single pretense of General Akechi's.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:29.590
Supported by the Imperial Court and temples, he exempts the people of tax to better their lives.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.460
General Akechi desires pacification of the realm.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.930
General Hashiba desires subjugation of the realm.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:41.310
The path to absolute justice lies with Akechi.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.880
The provinces surrounding Kyoto be pledged to Hashiba's cause!

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:49.150
Milord, I advise ye to better observe the fog.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.350
I shan't ignore the advice of my men.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.700
Though jeopardize the repute of Mikawa's warriors, such advice does.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:29.950
General Akechi, I march with 15,000 to assist ye.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:41.580
<b>June 13, 1582 {ts}</b>

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:41.580
<b>Yamashiro Province Oyamazaki {ts}</b>

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.240
Brother, our forces now occupy Mt. Tenno.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.970
Now superior, are our forces over Akechi's.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:54.630
Aye.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.520
Though General Takayama takes the honor of leading the vanguard,

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.640
I shall achieve greater prestige through leading the rear!

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.590
The enemy shall soon arrive!

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.380
My forces are to take defensive positions at Koizumi River!

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:11.960
Brother, over yonder!

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:22.470
At last, General Hashiba arrives...

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.700
with General Hidenaga and Lord Nobutaka in tow,

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.790
followed by General Niwa Nagahide's forces.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:32.470
The presence of Milord's kin and General Niwa
 assures our victory so.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:36.880
Might I make another request of ye generals?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:41.060
Hoist a banner of mine into battle.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.050
'Twill suffice to hoist one.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:55.440
What peculiar nature be of that symbol?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:01.700
Feel I naught but loss of integrity for my forces to hoist so queer a banner. {until saru dono}

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:06.990
Though we march to avenge Milord, I shan't heed such a request.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:10.870
General, I shall hoist said banner!

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:13.880
Speak your name.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:18.420
U-Ueda Satarou, General Hashiba.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:22.130
'Twas he who saw to the execution of Akechi's son, Tsuda Nobusumi.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.920
'Tis a most peculiar, yet intriguing banner I've beheld. {until kakkoyoi}

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.630
Perhaps, such a symbol be the sign of an era to forthcome.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.520
By whose hand was this symbol done?

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:36.430
'Twas Governor Furuta Sasuke, who governs a total of 400 koku.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.300
Ye shall have a banner.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:45.050
Won't ye stay thine tongue and be spared of shame?

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:47.790
Ye be not of an aesthete to judge, but of an uncouth warrior.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:52.170
'Twas aroused by the peculiar nature of such a banner.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.790
Furuta Sasuke...

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:00.040
What be the character of such a warrior?

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:12.770
Brother.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:13.260
Aye? {ugh?}

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.340
Be what of this fume?

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.300
Be of General Takayama's encampment.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.150
Endure this stench, I cannot!

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:24.820
Greetings, Brother!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:28.210
General, what do ye roast?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.660
Roast the meat of cattle, to feed the spirits of my men.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:35.290
'Twas from the Portuguese that I learned this.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:38.340
Though tradition be of a pot, a spade or breastplate may suffice. {until maniawase desuga}

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:43.300
Shall ye have a morsel, Brother? {until ohitotsu}

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.840
I shall.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.340
Brother!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.310
Be cleansed.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:53.350
Remove thine vambraces and purify thine hands.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:06.780
Known I had not of such an exquisite pairing of miso and ribs of cattle! {until omowananda}

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:12.140
Pique as this does an aesthete's tongue, shall I christen this roast an "aesthete's roast?" {until meishite wa}

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:22.210
Vigor ascends from the bowels and overwhelms my soul! {until kiyottazo}

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.130
Guard, fetch hot water!

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.640
Know this, General.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:40.020
The war to be fought shall surely rend the realm asunder! {until ooikusa}

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.230
Defeating the Wise General, Akechi Mitsuhide, {until to naraba}

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:45.780
requires vigor greater than that which cattle meat beckons!

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:48.530
Brother, ye use an excess of powder...

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.650
The brew shall serve to excel my vigor.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.540
Burn my visage unto thine eyes.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:58.790
'Tis the coming visage of the Lord of Aesthetes,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.630
the very visage of Furuta Sasuke's soul!

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.510
H-He is...

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:22.910
Furuta Sasuke?

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:51.340
Men!

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:54.600
Akechi's forces number 15,000!

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.780
Our forces number 40,000!

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:59.590
Men, our victory is assured!

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:05.730
Why does General Hashiba lead our forces?

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:10.760
'Tis the duty of the son, Lord Oda Nobutaka, to lead!

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.600
'Twas General Hashiba who amassed this force, Brother.

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:15.830
Nevertheless, we must take many more heads than they,

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.820
so the realm may know of our grand feats!

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:30.840
To overcome the disadvantage in men, capturing Mt. Tenno remains our imperative,

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:36.580
and I shall assault Nakagawa Kiyohide's
 defenses at its base.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:44.840
Saitou!

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:56.850
My gratitude...

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:20.270
We, men of General Akechi, shall defend Kyoto from the barbarous foe of the West!

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.830
They be a band of Banshu monkeys!

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:26.830
The strength of monkeys may ne'er be compared to that of men!

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.670
'Twas a fulfilling life we've lead.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.240
Though witnessed we have the ascension of Milord.

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:43.280
We shan't meet in the Afterlife!

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.630
Akechi's forces advance!

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:37.990
Arquebusiers, take aim!

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.210
Fire!

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:17.260
Charge!

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:18.770
Governor!

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.310
Our defensive line is worn!

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:37.270
Shall we request assistance from General Takayama, or withdraw?

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:38.460
Silence!

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:43.290
Nakagawa Kiyohide shan't borrow a hand from any in battle!

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:45.850
Henceforth, utter no such words of weakness!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.720
A true warrior prefers Death on the battlefield!

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.240
Master Yasuke!

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:11.880
I deliver unto ye truth.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:19.880
The intruder who fled from Honno Temple is here. {until ayashii otoko}

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:24.970
'Twas he who killed Nobu.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:31.390
Hashiba Hideyoshi.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.850
I care not what you do. {from shinjiru until kamawanai}

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:18.240
To Nobu, I have more to return.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.250
That... {sonna}

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:28.320
cannot be true!

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:37.540
General Hashiba's return from Takamatsu Castle was indeed <i>too</i> swift.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:41.400
Master Yasuke has naught to benefit from fabrications!

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.550
If so... {datosureba}

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:48.930
my true foe lies yonder! {ore no makoto no teki wa}

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:10.330
Feel resentment! {urame}

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.450
Feel anger!

00:19:12.530 --> 00:19:15.120
Deserving I am of such emotions!

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:38.670
Why... {naze da}

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.010
do I feel no resentment?!

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:51.070
I feel naught but overwhelmed by the fearsome character that is General Hashiba!

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:57.700
Governor Furuta, are ye harmed?!

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.330
General Hashiba be alike myself.

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:10.590
'Twas we who were nurtured by the grace of Milord since youthhood... {until hazu ga}

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:16.420
and yet, may General Hashiba meet Milord's grace with cruelty?!

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:26.110
May General Hashiba turn to cruelty for the sake of ruling the realm?!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:08.020
The time shall come when you must choose

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:15.830
whether or not to follow in my footsteps against a force which overwhelms your own. {from washi until washi no michi erabuka}

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.080
Or, shall you choose to serve your foes?

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:24.080
Survive, and ye shall see fair days.

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.190
Forsake him... {akirameyou}

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:53.940
Forsake Milord, {akiramate}

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.590
and live for thine self.

00:24:35.860 --> 00:24:37.480
<b>Now, we feast. {blue ts}</b>

00:24:47.990 --> 00:24:49.660
<b>It shan't be!</b>

00:24:49.660 --> 00:24:52.670
A Sorrowful Midnight Purple.

00:24:53.710 --> 00:24:58.300
Does the fork joining the aesthete and warrior exist?

00:24:56.540 --> 00:24:59.910
<b>A Sorrowful Midnight Purple{ts}</b>
